.Dd August 6, 2026
.Dt DOOR_CREATE 3C
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm door_create ,
.Nm door_xcreate
.Nd create a door descriptor
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In door.h
.Ft int
.Fo door_create
.Fa "door_server_procedure_t *server_procedure"
.Fa "void *cookie"
.Fa "uint_t attributes"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo door_xcreate
.Fa "door_server_procedure_t *server_procedure"
.Fa "void *cookie"
.Fa "uint_t attributes"
.Fa "door_xcreate_server_func_t *thr_create_func"
.Fa "door_xcreate_thrsetup_func_t *thr_setup_func"
.Fa "void *crcookie"
.Fa "int nthread"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn door_create
function creates a door descriptor that describes the procedure specified by
the function
.Fa server_procedure ,
which must be of the
.Vt door_server_procedure_t
type:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
typedef void door_server_procedure_t(void *cookie, char *argp,
    size_t arg_size, door_desc_t *dp, uint_t n_desc);
.Ed
.Pp
The data item,
.Fa cookie ,
is associated with the door descriptor, and is passed as an argument to the
invoked function
.Fa server_procedure
during
.Xr door_call 3C
invocations.
Other arguments passed to
.Fa server_procedure
from an associated
.Fn door_call
are placed on the stack and include
.Fa argp
and
.Fa dp .
The
.Fa argp
argument points to
.Fa arg_size
bytes of data and the
.Fa dp
argument points to
.Fa n_desc
.Vt door_desc_t
structures.
The
.Fa attributes
argument specifies attributes associated with the newly created door.
Valid values for
.Fa attributes
are constructed by OR-ing one or more of the following values:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Dv DOOR_UNREF
Delivers a special invocation on the door when the number of descriptors that
refer to this door drops to one.
In order to trigger this condition, more than one descriptor must have referred
to this door at some time.
.Dv DOOR_UNREF_DATA
designates an unreferenced invocation, as the
.Fa argp
argument passed to
.Fa server_procedure .
In the case of an unreferenced invocation, the values for
.Fa arg_size ,
.Fa dp
and
.Fa n_desc
are
.Sy 0 .
Only one unreferenced invocation is delivered on behalf of a door.
.It Dv DOOR_UNREF_MULTI
Similar to
.Dv DOOR_UNREF ,
except multiple unreferenced invocations can be delivered on the same door if
the number of descriptors referring to the door drops to one more than once.
Since an additional reference may have been passed by the time an unreferenced
invocation arrives, the
.Dv DOOR_IS_UNREF
attribute returned by the
.Xr door_info 3C
call can be used to determine if the door is still unreferenced.
.It Dv DOOR_PRIVATE
Maintains a separate pool of server threads on behalf of the door.
Server threads are associated with a door's private server pool using
.Xr door_bind 3C .
.It Dv DOOR_REFUSE_DESC
Any attempt to call
.Xr door_call 3C
on this door with argument descriptors will fail with
.Er ENOTSUP .
When this flag is set, the door's server procedure will always be invoked with
an
.Fa n_desc
argument of 0.
.It Dv DOOR_NO_CANCEL
Clients which abort calls to
.Fn door_call
on this door will not cause the cancellation of the server thread handling the
request.
See
.Xr cancellation 7 .
.El
.Pp
The descriptor returned from
.Fn door_create
and
.Fn door_xcreate
will be marked as close on exec
.Pq Dv FD_CLOEXEC .
Information about a door is available for all clients of a door using
.Fn door_info .
Applications concerned with security should not place secure information in
door data that is accessible by
.Fn door_info .
In particular, secure data should not be stored in the data item
.Fa cookie .
.Pp
By default, additional threads are created as needed to handle concurrent
.Fn door_call
invocations of doors created with
.Fn door_create .
See
.Xr door_server_create 3C
for information on how to change this behavior.
The server threads of doors created with
.Fn door_xcreate
are managed as described below.
.Pp
A process can advertise a door in the file system name space using
.Xr fattach 3C .
.Pp
After creation,
.Xr door_setparam 3C
can be used to set limits on the amount of data and descriptors clients can
send over the door.
.Ss door_xcreate()
The
.Fn door_xcreate
function creates a door as
.Fn door_create
does, but with a private pool of server threads whose creation and attributes
are under the control of the application.
In addition to the attributes described above,
.Fa attributes
may include the following value, which is not supported by
.Fn door_create :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Dv DOOR_NO_DEPLETION_CB
The
.Fa thr_create_func
function is called to create the initial pool of server threads only.
It is not called again when the pool is found to be depleted.
.El
.Pp
The
.Fa thr_create_func
and
.Fa thr_setup_func
arguments are pointers to functions of the following types:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
typedef int door_xcreate_server_func_t(door_info_t *dip,
    void *(*startf)(void *), void *startfarg, void *crcookie);

typedef void door_xcreate_thrsetup_func_t(void *crcookie);
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Fa thr_create_func
function is called once for each server thread that is required, with
.Fa dip
pointing to a
.Vt door_info_t
that identifies the door, and with the
.Fa crcookie
argument that was passed to
.Fn door_xcreate .
It must attempt to create one new thread that runs the start function
.Fa startf
with the argument
.Fa startfarg ,
passing both to
.Xr thr_create 3C
or
.Xr pthread_create 3C
unmodified.
The new thread must be created detached, and may otherwise be configured as
the application wishes, for example with a different stack size or signal
mask.
The
.Fa thr_create_func
function must return 1 on success, -1 if thread creation failed, and 0 if
no more server threads should be created at this time.
.Pp
During the call to
.Fn door_xcreate ,
.Fa thr_create_func
is called
.Fa nthread
times to create the door's initial pool of server threads.
.Fa nthread
must be at least 1.
All
.Fa nthread
threads must be created successfully and bind to the door's private pool,
otherwise
.Fn door_xcreate
fails and any threads that were created exit.
Unless the door was created with
.Dv DOOR_NO_DEPLETION_CB ,
.Fa thr_create_func
is subsequently called again each time a door invocation finds all of the
threads in the pool busy, giving the application the opportunity to grow the
pool.
These depletion callbacks can be distinguished from initial pool creation by
the presence of
.Dv DOOR_DEPLETION_CB
in the
.Fa di_attributes
member of the
.Vt door_info_t
to which
.Fa dip
points.
Returning 0 from
.Fa thr_create_func
during a depletion callback is not an error, and can be used to limit the
size of the pool.
A door invocation that finds no available server thread waits in the kernel
until one becomes free.
.Pp
If
.Fa thr_setup_func
is not
.Dv NULL ,
each new server thread calls it with
.Fa crcookie
before binding to the door's private pool.
This can be used to perform once-only thread configuration such as
setting up thread-specific data or blocking signals.
If
.Fa thr_setup_func
is
.Dv NULL ,
the thread has POSIX thread cancellation disabled, as for threads created
by the default server thread creation function.
The thread then binds to the door's private pool and makes itself available
to service invocations.
The application does not call
.Xr door_bind 3C
or
.Xr door_return 3C
itself.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Upon successful completion,
.Fn door_create
and
.Fn door_xcreate
return a non-negative value.
Otherwise, they return -1 and set
.Va errno
to indicate the error.
If
.Fn door_xcreate
fails, no door is created and no new server threads remain.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Sy Example 1
Create a door and use
.Fn fattach
to advertise the door in the file system namespace.
.Pp
The following example creates a door and uses
.Fn fattach
to advertise the door in the file system namespace.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
void
server(void *cookie, char *argp, size_t arg_size, door_desc_t *dp,
    uint_t n_desc)
{
    door_return(NULL, 0, NULL, 0);
    /* NOTREACHED */
}

int
main(int argc, char *argv[])
{
    int did;
    struct stat buf;

    if ((did = door_create(server, 0, 0)) < 0) {
        perror("door_create");
        exit(1);
    }

    /* make sure file system location exists */
    if (stat("/tmp/door", &buf) < 0) {
        int newfd;
        if ((newfd = creat("/tmp/door", 0444)) < 0) {
            perror("creat");
            exit(1);
        }
        (void) close(newfd);
    }

    /* make sure nothing else is attached */
    (void) fdetach("/tmp/door");

    /* attach to file system */
    if (fattach(did, "/tmp/door") < 0) {
        perror("fattach");
        exit(2);
    }
    [...]
}
.Ed
.Pp
.Sy Example 2
Create a door with a bounded pool of server threads.
.Pp
The following example uses
.Fn door_xcreate
to create a door that is serviced by a fixed pool of four threads with a
smaller stack size than the default.
Since the door is created with
.Dv DOOR_NO_DEPLETION_CB ,
the pool never grows beyond its initial size.
The server procedure is as shown in the first example.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static pthread_attr_t attr;

static int
create_server_thread(door_info_t *dip, void *(*startf)(void *),
    void *startfarg, void *crcookie)
{
    if (pthread_create(NULL, &attr, startf, startfarg) != 0)
        return (-1);
    return (1);
}

int
main(int argc, char *argv[])
{
    int did;

    (void) pthread_attr_init(&attr);
    (void) pthread_attr_setdetachstate(&attr, PTHREAD_CREATE_DETACHED);
    (void) pthread_attr_setstacksize(&attr, 128 * 1024);

    did = door_xcreate(server, NULL, DOOR_NO_DEPLETION_CB,
        create_server_thread, NULL, NULL, 4);
    if (did < 0) {
        perror("door_xcreate");
        exit(1);
    }
    [...]
}
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
The
.Fn door_create
and
.Fn door_xcreate
functions will fail if:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Er EINVAL
Invalid attributes are passed.
This includes passing
.Dv DOOR_NO_DEPLETION_CB
to
.Fn door_create .
.It Er EMFILE
The process has too many open descriptors.
.It Er ENOTSUP
The function was called from a
.Xr vfork 2
child.
.El
.Pp
The
.Fn door_xcreate
function will additionally fail if:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Er E2BIG
The
.Fa nthread
argument is too large.
.It Er EBADF
A newly created server thread could not bind to the door's private pool.
.It Er EINVAL
The
.Fa nthread
argument is less than 1,
.Fa thr_create_func
is
.Dv NULL ,
or
.Fa thr_create_func
returned 0 during the creation of the initial thread pool.
.It Er ENOMEM
Memory allocation failed.
.It Er EPIPE
The
.Fa thr_create_func
function returned -1.
.El
.Sh INTERFACE STABILITY
.Sy Committed
.Sh MT-LEVEL
.Sy Safe
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vfork 2 ,
.Xr door_bind 3C ,
.Xr door_call 3C ,
.Xr door_info 3C ,
.Xr door_return 3C ,
.Xr door_revoke 3C ,
.Xr door_server_create 3C ,
.Xr door_setparam 3C ,
.Xr fattach 3C ,
.Xr pthread_create 3C ,
.Xr thr_create 3C ,
.Xr libdoor 3LIB ,
.Xr attributes 7 ,
.Xr cancellation 7
